00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.590 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it was the hot  summer of 2019 i was at the khan  film festival attending a world premiere  and leonardo dicaprio was clapping for  me  yes i know well not just for me  as you may know leonardo dicaprio is a  u.n messenger for peace  with a special focus on climate change  his project at khan was a new  documentary  on global warming ice on fire  instead of the usual doom and gloom you  might expect  his documentary took a new approach  it showcased the work of real scientists  measuring co2 emissions in hawaii  researchers monitoring methane leaks in  alaska  and engineers inventing technologies  that fight climate change  and i was one of those engineers  the technology i helped create and  develop  called direct air capture was featured  in leonardo's documentary  and yes i called him leonardo we're  close  while i'm not here to promote ice on  fire you should probably still check it  out  rather i'm here to talk to you about  what i expect i will be doing for my  entire life  i'm here to talk to you about the good  the bad  and the absolute necessity of direct air  capture  as the name suggests director capture  uses machines  to capture carbon dioxide or co2  from the air these machines use air  which contain 0.04 percent co2  and deliver 100 concentrated co2  the pure co2 can be used as a chemical  building block  for other materials like plastics or  synthetic fuels  but the vast majority of it must be  stored underground for good  how do these machines work there are  several technologies out there  but they all have chemistry at their  core and they all have the same goal  to capture and remove carbon dioxide  from the air  but let's look at it step by step and i  am an engineer so i will be going into  all the gory details  in a first step big fans bring air in  contact with the filter  that you can imagine as a sponge  the filter continuously and selectively  takes up co2 from the air until the  sponge is saturated  in a second step the co2  is unloaded from the filter either using  heat  or pressure this is where we squeeze the  sponge  so that we can use it again once free of  co2  the filter can be ready for another  loading and unloading cycle  the final result is pure co2  from the air and better yet  atmospheric air would reduce co2  concentrations  hope you're still with me and that you  have a good idea of how this all works  now you might be wondering well there's  a lot of  air out there and at only 0.04  co2 well director capture  sounds like looking for a needle in a  haystack  why bother to understand  why we need to look at the current state  of climate change  and here the doom and gloom are frankly  justified the world  has emitted so much co2 that most  climate models  show that global warming cannot be kept  to the original  1.5 degree temperature limit  the good news there are current efforts  underway  to decarbonize the economy electric cars  solar panels windmills these will help  reduce  the amount of co2 we put into the  atmosphere  the bad news there is no off  switch we cannot stop emissions tomorrow  even if we wanted to this can only be  a gradual process  so we need director capture  and this is where director capture comes  into play  to remove historic legacy emissions  and to help our increasing efforts of  decarbonization  we need director capture with co2  storage  underground so that all the excess co2  from the atmosphere  is stored away for good  i want to acknowledge as for some of you  putting co2 back underground sounds like  a worrying prospect  people ask me is there space underground  is it safe will the co2 just leak back  out  that's because we mostly imagined earth  as a solid ball  dense and compact but that's not the  case  we know there is space for the co2  underground because that's where it came  from  in the first place from natural gas  oil and coal that we've mined and burned  so what are the benefits of director  capture what does this do for us  first we can control how many machines  we build  and how fast we build them second their  efficiency  and their performance can be measured  and we can easily track and certify  how much co2 we've removed this  technology  gives us control over our climate change  mitigation strategy  but why do we need director capture if  we have trees  and other natural solutions and here  it's not an either or we need both  we need as many large forests as  possible  to capture co2 and keep it in the carbon  natural cycle  carbon natural cycle already relies on  soils  forests and the oceans to keep co2 out  of the atmosphere  but that's not enough forest cannot be  large enough  to keep all the co2 all the excess co2  that we have  worse even is that climate change and  human behavior affect forests  and today we are losing more trees than  we're adding  so we need director capture something  that even the critics of this technology  can acknowledge and what do the critics  say  some say co2 removal or technological  carbon removal  should be our last resort and it is  it is one of the last few lifeboats we  have  and we should use it and  by the way life votes are good i suspect  leonardo himself  would have used one on the titanic had  it been available  other critics worry about the moral  hazards of this technology  especially problematic is if companies  or governments  use the mere possibility of direct air  capture  as an excuse to postpone co2 emission  reductions  but let's be clear the pledge to remove  carbon dioxide in the future should not  be allowed  to embolden emitters today and this is  where we need  good policy i'm the first to admit  that engineering and building director  capture machines  my life's work is only but a small piece  of what is needed to undo decades of  reckless co2 emissions  but this is why i'm here today to ask  for your help  director capture needs you as well to  find the right policies  the right financial incentives and even  the right regulations  and while i cannot promise too much  glory  or applause at khan or otherwise  i can promise you it will be earth  changing  thank you

